From 7ecdd4e84281d84c5adf3453d776f078261613f4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@lccc.local>
Date: Sat, 29 Aug 2026 12:09:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] x86-64: fold single-use widening casts into narrow
 compares (PF-15)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

`(int)a < (int)b` on char/short operands widened BOTH operands to
32/64-bit and then executed a 32/64-bit compare — three extension moves
where GCC emits one `cmpb`/`cmpw` on the original bytes (its `scmp`
shape: xorl/cmpb/setl/ret). Byte-sized comparisons are ubiquitous in
real code (string/protocol parsers, zlib longest_match inner loops);
every one paid two dead widening moves plus a wide compare.

Mechanism — defer, then fold at the compare:

* A single-use widening Cast (I8/U8/I16/U16 -> 32/64-bit) with a GPR
  destination and a reg- or slot-homed source DEFERS its extending move
  (two pending slots) instead of emitting it.

* The consuming Cmp folds the recorded pair into ONE narrow compare on
  the original sources; a constant rhs folds too when it fits the
  narrow domain exactly. Anything else flushes the recorded moves
  unchanged, so the defer is invisible to every non-matching consumer.

* Flag-exactness matrix (proved in the code): sext+sext keeps the
  signed setcc family (sign extension is order-preserving); zext+zext
  maps every opcode onto the unsigned family (zero-extended values are
  non-negative, where signed and unsigned order coincide); mixed
  extensions and out-of-domain constants are refused and materialize
  the widens instead.

Soundness (the three hazards, each with an explicit guard):

* Home clobbering between defer and consume: RA may reuse the first
  source's register for the second cast's destination once the source's
  only modelled use (the deferred move) ends its live range. The record
  path refuses (and flushes) when a later cast's destination equals an
  earlier deferred source's register. The reversed aliasing is
  impossible: the two SSA ranges overlap by construction. Slot sources
  are safe because nothing is emitted between record and consume.

* Dispatch bypass: fusion paths, MachInst queueing, and the instruction
  dispatch all bypass each other, so the flush/fold discipline lives at
  the single per-instruction loop head every lowering path shares. The
  fold happens BEFORE MachInst sees the compare; folded compares emit on
  the classic path, so MachInst's audited gates are untouched.

* Lost records: every refusal path that has already taken records
  re-emits the taken widening moves explicitly; take-pair restores on
  any mismatch. A deferred move can never silently vanish.

Unsigned widening casts are gated away from MachInst ISel when they
match the defer shape (the mature path is the pre-MachInst default, so
the gate only routes work back to audited code; try_record re-checks
every condition and emits normally on any mismatch).

The compare itself emits through the existing typed emitter, so slot
and register sources keep all existing addressing behaviour.

Validated: exhaustive byte-domain suites (all 8 compare shapes x all
65536 input pairs) and strided 16-bit suites pass bit-identically to
GCC; new regression test tests/regression/byte_cmp_narrow.c pins the
shapes end-to-end against GCC; lib gate 1302 passed / 0 failed under
-D warnings; x86-64 regression corpus 960 passed / 0 failed; i686
corpus unchanged at its known 403/76 (separate backend); godbolt
x86-64 oracle census unchanged (6278 vs GCC 5773 instructions, same
per-program profile as the pre-change baseline). Trace: CCC_DEBUG_PF15.
